WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:06.620
OK, I'm finding myself very annoyed by a portion
of the left that thinks anybody being cautious

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:12.249
about the polling for Donald Trump versus
Joe Biden is doing some kind of reverse gaslighting

00:00:12.249 --> 00:00:13.799
or concern trolling.

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:16.039
I am here to tell you guys right now.

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:17.860
Cut it.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.620
We have to stop it or we're going to lose.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.960
Donald Trump can easily end up winning reelection.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.460
Now, when I say this, I'm not saying Trump
is definitely winning right now despite the

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.460
polling.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.300
I'm not saying the polling is wrong.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.480
What I am saying is that a small change between
now and November could easily end up with

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:39.500
Donald Trump winning the Electoral College
while still losing the popular vote.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.739
Every time I point this out, I get more and
more people e-mailing me saying, David, stop,

00:00:43.739 --> 00:00:45.280
reverse gaslighting us.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.770
You're making us think Biden will lose.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.489
So that we go out and vote when in reality,
Biden has this locked up.

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:54.329
First of all, Joe Biden does not have this
locked up.

00:00:54.329 --> 00:00:55.940
And I'm going to present the facts to you.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:00:57.149
Let's do it step by step.

00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:00.420
Number one, national polling trend lines.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.420
Yes.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.900
Joe Biden right now is winning the national
polls by an average of seven.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.220
But two days ago it was eight, and two months
ago it was 10.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:12.820
So the lead is shrinking for Joe Biden now.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.820
OK.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.320
You might say fine.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.930
Joe Biden's winning by seven instead of 10.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.310
But seven is a huge lead in the popular vote.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.650
Well, that's true.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:26.990
But let me remind you that on this day in
2016, you go back and look at the polling,

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:28.409
Trump versus Hillary.

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:31.170
August 27, 2016.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.030
Hillary was winning by six point three.

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:39.500
So the difference between today and 2016 is
zero point seven points.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.500
Biden's plus seven right now.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.170
Hillary four years ago today was plus six
point three.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:47.920
And Trump won electorally in 2016.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:53.030
I don't know about you, but zero point seven
points is not exactly something that makes

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:54.930
me feel particularly confident.

00:01:54.930 --> 00:02:01.090
If it comes down to zero point seven percentage
points in November 3rd, comparing to 2016

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:02.090
to 2020.

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.619
Like, for example, Hillary won the popular
vote by two point one.

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:09.229
If Biden wins by 2.8, he can still lose.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.229
He can still lose.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.229
So this is not a joke.

00:02:11.229 --> 00:02:12.620
This is not gaslighting.

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.260
This is not concern trolling.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.380
And pollsters are noticing 538.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.560
Nate Silver tweeted about it yesterday.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:24.000
He tweeted, quote, Biden's Electoral College
win probability down a bit to 70 percent after

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.180
some mediocre polls for him this morning.

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:28.230
He had been hovering around 73 percent.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.280
So not a big shift, but worth a quick Twitter
thread.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.840
And Nate Silver went on later in the same
thread to say, quote, Biden has gotten some

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:38.870
not so spectacular swing state polls lately.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:42.840
His lead in Florida is down to five point
four and Pennsylvania to five point eight,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:45.270
which remain the most likely tipping point
states.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:51.069
Not bad, but the Electoral College popular
vote gap would appear to be widening a bit.

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:56.209
And then later yesterday, Nate Silver tweeted,
quote, Fundamentally, the fundamentals are

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.590
improving for Trump.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.190
The economy is getting better, although that
could be threatened by congressional inaction.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:06.489
Cold cases are going down, although that could
reverse itself at pretty much any time.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:09.790
This is exactly the case I've been making
for two to three months now.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:16.400
Presidential prognosticator Allan Lichtman
recently said all of his qualitative indicators

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.769
point to Biden.

00:03:17.769 --> 00:03:19.980
It still looks OK for Biden.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.159
So what do you want to take a chance on that
and then add to this voter suppression that

00:03:25.159 --> 00:03:26.590
we know they will do?

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:30.190
The funny business with the post office that
they are doing already.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.010
Early voting starts soon.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.550
You should go do it.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.090
Find your plan.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.849
Are you going to vote in person?

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:40.840
Are you going to wear, you know, three masks
and a hazmat suit and vote in person?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.180
Are you going to get an absentee ballot and
send it in by mail?

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:46.989
Are you getting an absentee ballot and dropping
it off?

00:03:46.989 --> 00:03:47.989
Have a plan.

00:03:47.989 --> 00:03:54.379
We must operate under the assumption that
Trump could win any state by one vote.

00:03:54.379 --> 00:03:58.580
And based on that, every single person should
be voting and assuming nothing.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:03:59.880
This is not concern trolling.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.560
These are the numbers.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:02.560
Let me know what you think.

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:02.809
I'm on Twitter at David Pakman.

